  "conclusion": "Anchors 1 and 2 have channel-independent H-only race cuts whose fixed loss is below their immutable reference floor. No choice of stochastic Q, deterministic map, task decoder, gradient optimizer, or additional optimization iterations can satisfy the unchanged delta=0 registered banks. The archived fallback Q is feasible only after the explicitly recorded common relaxation and is ineligible for a registered-feasible all-anchor C2 nomination. Even the most permissive registered P1 delta=+0.002 leaves single-cut deficits 0.006016457721568226 (anchor 1) and 0.00363754540267114 (anchor 2); delta=-0.002 is stricter. The unrun noncenter P1 units are analytic not-triggered implications, not executed outcomes. No floor or role was moved.",
